{
  "schema": 3,
  "description": "Batch 6: the exemption set, attacked from the inside. Every case takes a head that capability.ts had already decided not to judge - a data-tail member, a toolchain, a policy head the rules layer owns - and asks it to do the worst thing it can do. Two findings generalise: a read-only claim only holds until a flag writes (sort -o, less -o, rg --pre, man -P), and an exemption is not a statement that the rest of the line is harmless. The last block is ordinary work that must stay pass, because a false ask on it makes the write and shell tools unusable wherever no approval UI is composed.",
